Equivalent Expressions 3|3.19|433184f1|392|D|mcq|-|Which is equivalent to 4/(4x-5)-1/(x+1)?|1/((x+1)(4x-5));3/(3x-6);-1/((x+1)(4x-5));9/((x+1)(4x-5))|Numerator 4(x+1)-(4x-5)=9; A=numerator 1; B=subtracted numerators and denominators separately; C=sign error; D=CORRECT
Equivalent Expressions 3|3.20|c3b116d7|424|B|mcq|roman-numeral|Which is(are) a factor of 3x^2+20x-63? I. x-9  II. 3x-7|I only;II only;I and II;Neither|Factors are (3x-7)(x+9); I is wrong sign; B=II only CORRECT; C/D=misfactored
Evaluating Statistical Claims 1|1.1|9bf4c545|469|D|mcq|-|City council surveyed 500 residents who own dogs about a dog park. Which is true about the survey?|Shows majority of residents favor;Should have included more dog owners;Should have been entirely non-dog-owners;Sample is biased because not representative|A=overgeneralizes from a biased sample; B=would worsen the bias; C=overcorrects to the opposite bias; D=CORRECT
Evaluating Statistical Claims 1|1.2|82dfb646|469|D|mcq|-|200 people chosen at random from people who liked a book watched the movie; 95% disliked it. Which inference is appropriate?|95% of moviegoers will dislike;95% of book readers will dislike;Most who dislike the book will like the movie;Most who like the book will dislike the movie|Inference limited to the sampled population (people who liked the book); A/B=wrong population; C=reverses the group; D=CORRECT
Evaluating Statistical Claims 2|2.1|37930b2a|515|A|mcq|roman-numeral|Random sample of 200 town residents, 87% satisfied. Which must be true? I. 87% of all residents satisfied  II. Another sample of 200 would also give 87%|Neither;I only;II only;I and II|A sample proportion neither equals the parameter nor repeats exactly; A=Neither CORRECT; B/C/D=treat the sample statistic as exact
Evaluating Statistical Claims 2|2.2|b4f5a7ca|444|C|mcq|-|Sample of history professors selected at random from the California State Universities. Largest population to generalize to?|All professors in the US;All history professors in the US;All history professors at all CSUs;All professors at all CSUs|Generalize only to the sampled frame; A/B=too broad; C=CORRECT; D=broader than the sampled subgroup
Evaluating Statistical Claims 2|2.3|642519d7|609|A|mcq|roman-numeral|1000 adults selected at random from a large city, 78% satisfied with air quality. Which must be true? (1 population equals 78, 2 another sample gives 78, 3 a different city gives 78)|None;II only;I and II only;I and III only|No statement must be true: sampling variability and a different population; A=CORRECT
Evaluating Statistical Claims 3|3.1|1ea09200|469|B|mcq|-|Random sample of 40 fourth-grade students from a certain school. Largest population the results apply to?|The 40 students;All fourth-grade students at the school;All students at the school;All fourth-graders in the county|A=too narrow (sample itself); B=CORRECT; C/D=broader than the sampling frame
Evaluating Statistical Claims 3|3.2|7d68096f|686|D|mcq|two-way-table|55 teams selected at random from all trivia teams in a tournament; table shows the 40 that practiced 3+ hours. Largest population to generalize to?|Teams scoring 14+;The 55 teams in the sample;The 40 teams practicing 3+ hours;All trivia teams in the tournament|Random selection was from all teams in the tournament; A/C=subgroups shown in the table; B=the sample itself; D=CORRECT
Evaluating Statistical Claims 3|3.3|7ce2830a|542|B|mcq|-|Random sample of 35 students from all students at one middle school in a large city. Largest group to generalize to?|The 35 students;All students at the school;All middle school students in the city;All students in the city|A=the sample; B=CORRECT; C/D=broader than the school sampled
Evaluating Statistical Claims 3|3.4|aa43b41f|493|B|mcq|-|Cable news website poll: 28% Yes, 70% No. Why are results unlikely to represent the US population?|Percentages do not add to 100;Respondents were not a random sample;Not 50-50 split;Not enough time to respond|A=irrelevant (undecided exist); B=voluntary response bias CORRECT; C/D=irrelevant to representativeness
Evaluating Statistical Claims 3|3.5|4a422e3e|518|C|mcq|-|Tabitha surveyed 20 families at a playground to find mean children per household; mean was 2.4. Which must be true?|Community mean is 2.4;Should not determine because sample too small;Sampling method is flawed and may be biased;Method is not flawed and likely unbiased|A=treats a convenience sample as the population; B=blames size rather than the real flaw; C=CORRECT (playground oversamples families with children); D=opposite
Evaluating Statistical Claims 3|3.6|6fca0144|465|D|mcq|-|50 baobab trees aged 17 randomly selected in a habitat, randomly assigned to two watering groups. Largest group results apply to?|The 50 trees selected;All 19-year-old trees in the habitat;All 17-year-old trees in South Africa;All 17-year-old trees in this habitat|A=the sample; B=wrong age; C=broader than the habitat sampled; D=CORRECT
Linear Equations in One Variable 1|1.1|097e10f5|369|A|mcq|-|What value of p satisfies the equation 5p+180=250?|14;65;86;250|A=(250-180)/5 CORRECT; B=250/5-... (divided before subtracting incorrectly); C=misc; D=copied the constant
Linear Equations in One Variable 1|1.2|997bec28|242|35|spr|-|The perimeter of an isosceles triangle is 83 inches. Each of the two congruent sides is 24 inches. What is the third side?|-|SPR: 83-2(24)=35; error 59 (subtracted one side only)
Linear Equations in One Variable 1|1.3|6ac23de7|444|A|mcq|-|4x/5=20. What is x?|25;24;16;15|A=20*5/4 CORRECT; B=misc; C=20*4/5 (inverted the fraction); D=20-5
Linear Equations in One Variable 1|1.4|7392dfc1|427|D|mcq|-|Which is equivalent to 4x+6=12?|2x+4=6;x+3=3;3x+2=4;2x+3=6|A=divided only some terms by 2; B=divided inconsistently; C=divided by different numbers; D=divided every term by 2 CORRECT
Linear Equations in One Variable 1|1.5|93954cfa|450|A|mcq|-|One pound of grapes costs $2. How many dollars will c pounds cost?|2c;2+c;2/c;c/2|A=CORRECT; B=added instead of multiplying; C/D=divided (rate inverted)
Linear Equations in One Variable 1|1.6|3d04de9c|393|A|mcq|-|A principal used 25 flags total, blue or yellow, and 20 were blue. How many yellow flags?|5;20;25;30|A=25-20 CORRECT; B=copied blue count; C=copied total; D=added
Linear Equations in One Variable 1|1.7|60f71697|394|A|mcq|-|8x=88. What value of x is the solution?|11;80;96;704|A=88/8 CORRECT; B=88-8; C=88+8; D=88*8
Linear Equations in One Variable 1|1.8|550b352c|428|B|mcq|-|10=2x+4. How many solutions exist?|None;Exactly 1;Exactly 3;Infinitely many|A linear equation with one variable term has exactly one solution; B=CORRECT; A/C/D=confuse with no-solution or identity cases
Linear Equations in One Variable 1|1.9|ed18c4f7|419|D|mcq|-|Cathy has n CDs. Gerry has 3 more than twice the number Cathy has. In terms of n, how many CDs does Gerry have?|3n-2;3n+2;2n-3;2n+3|A/B=swapped the roles of 2 and 3; C=subtracted instead of adding; D=CORRECT
Linear Equations in One Variable 1|1.10|12255364|418|C|mcq|-|A gym charges a onetime 36 dollar enrollment fee and 19 dollars per month. After how many months is the total 188 dollars?|4;5;8;10|Solve 36+19m=188; A/B=too few months; C=CORRECT; D=ignored the enrollment fee
Linear Equations in One Variable 1|1.11|d9d83c02|471|D|mcq|-|For what value of w does w-10=2(w+5)?|5;0;-15;-20|Distribute then isolate; A/B/C=sign or distribution errors; D=-20 CORRECT
Linear Equations in One Variable 1|1.12|7a987ae4|428|B|mcq|-|If 2n/5=10, what is the value of 2n-1?|24;49;50;99|2n=50 so 2n-1=49; A=solved for n then subtracted; C=gave 2n; D=doubled twice; B=CORRECT
Linear Equations in One Variable 1|1.13|9ff10b3b|512|C|mcq|-|If (1/2)x-(1/6)x=1, what is the value of x?|-4;1/3;3;6|Combine to (1/3)x=1; A/B=inverted or sign error; C=CORRECT; D=used 1/6 only
Linear Equations in One Variable 1|1.14|4e77195b|217|480|spr|-|If 2+x=60, what is the value of 16+8x?|-|SPR: 8(2+x)=8(60)=480
Linear Equations in One Variable 1|1.15|4f7981a0|249|24|spr|-|If 3x+2=8, what is the value of 9x+6?|-|SPR: 3(3x+2)=3(8)=24
Linear Equations in One Variable 1|1.16|46f68129|417|B|mcq|-|A librarian has 43 books. Giving each child 2 books leaves 7 books left over. How many children are in the group?|15;18;25;29|Solve 2c+7=43; A/C/D=added instead of subtracting or divided wrong; B=18 CORRECT
Linear Equations in One Variable 1|1.17|e53870b6|274|5|spr|-|6x+k=6x+5 has infinitely many solutions. What is the value of k?|-|SPR: k=5 (constants must match)
Linear Equations in One Variable 1|1.18|70774aa4|369|D|mcq|-|If 5x=20, what is the value of 15x?|7;12;23;60|Multiply both sides by 3; A/B/C=solved for x then mis-scaled; D=60 CORRECT
Linear Equations in One Variable 1|1.19|a9c04a21|401|C|mcq|-|What is the solution to the equation 2x+3=7?|1;1.5;2;4|A/B=divided before subtracting; C=CORRECT; D=subtracted only
Linear Equations in One Variable 1|1.20|590f2187|391|B|mcq|-|If 3x-27=24, what is the value of x-9?|1;8;24;35|Divide the whole equation by 3; A/C/D=solved for x or copied a constant; B=8 CORRECT
Linear Equations in One Variable 1|1.21|59afe8db|391|A|mcq|-|3x+5(x+4)=76. What value of x is the solution?|7;8;56;72|Distribute then solve 8x+20=76; A=7 CORRECT; B=off by one; C/D=partial results before dividing
Linear Equations in One Variable 1|1.22|c7d7980e|223|8|spr|-|13x=112-x. What value of x is the solution?|-|SPR: 14x=112 so x=8
Linear Equations in One Variable 1|1.23|40ba6288|391|B|mcq|-|If 3x=30, what is the value of 3x-12?|-2;18;22;42|Substitute 30 directly; A/C=solved for x first; B=18 CORRECT; D=added
Linear Equations in One Variable 1|1.24|87071893|242|55|spr|-|x+40=95. What value of x is the solution?|-|SPR: 55
Linear Equations in One Variable 1|1.25|3c4ce699|217|27|spr|-|If 6+x=9, what is the value of 18+3x?|-|SPR: 3(6+x)=3(9)=27
Linear Equations in One Variable 1|1.26|4de87c9a|370|D|mcq|-|3 more than 8 times a number x is equal to 83. Which equation represents this situation?|(3)(8)x=83;8x=83+3;3x+8=83;8x+3=83|A=multiplied both numbers; B=moved the 3 to the wrong side; C=swapped coefficient and constant; D=CORRECT
Linear Equations in One Variable 1|1.27|8339793c|266|10|spr|-|Nasir bought 9 storage bins at the same price, used a 63 dollar coupon, and paid 27 dollars total. What was the original price of 1 bin?|-|SPR: 9p-63=27 so p=10
Linear Equations in One Variable 1|1.28|2f0a43b2|222|0.2|spr|-|If x/8=5, what is the value of 8/x?|-|SPR: x=40 so 8/40=0.2; error 5 (inverted the equation instead)
Linear Equations in One Variable 1|1.29|4f8bd093|381|D|mcq|-|What value of x is the solution to 16x+24=24x?|-4;3/10;1/3;3|Collect x terms to get 24=8x; A/B/C=sign or division errors; D=3 CORRECT
Linear Equations in One Variable 1|1.30|9b886541|381|D|mcq|-|If 3x-8=7, what is the value of 3x+8?|-1;5;13;23|3x=15 so 3x+8=23; A/B=solved for x; C=added 8 to x not 3x; D=CORRECT
Linear Equations in One Variable 2|2.1|7a5a74a6|578|B|mcq|-|3(2x-6)-11=4(x-3)+6. If x is the solution, what is the value of x-3?|23/2;17/2;15/2;-15/2|x=23/2 so x-3=17/2; A=gave x itself; C/D=arithmetic or sign slips; B=CORRECT
Linear Equations in One Variable 2|2.2|aa85b138|478|B|mcq|-|2n+6=14 models a tree planted at 6 feet reaching 14 feet in n years. Best interpretation of the 2?|Years to double its height;Average feet the tree grew per year;Height in feet at 1 year old;Average years for similar trees to grow 14 feet|The 2 is the rate of change; A/C/D=misread slope as a time or an initial value; B=CORRECT
Linear Equations in One Variable 2|2.3|15daa8d6|242|2|spr|-|2x+16=a(x+8) has infinitely many solutions. What is the value of a?|-|SPR: a=2
Linear Equations in One Variable 2|2.4|12ee1edc|425|A|mcq|-|(b-2)x=8 has no solution. What is the value of b?|2;4;6;10|No solution requires the x-coefficient to vanish while the constant does not; A=2 CORRECT; B/C/D=arbitrary
Linear Equations in One Variable 2|2.5|70e29454|452|B|mcq|-|a(3-x)-b=-1-2x has infinitely many solutions. What are the values of a and b?|a=2 and b=1;a=2 and b=7;a=-2 and b=5;a=-2 and b=-5|Match coefficients: -a=-2 and 3a-b=-1; A=wrong b; C/D=sign error on a; B=CORRECT
Linear Equations in One Variable 2|2.6|f09097b1|364|22.4|spr|-|A corn plant grew an average of 1.20 cm per day for 12 days, ending at 36.8 cm. What was the height at the beginning?|-|SPR: 36.8-12(1.20)=22.4
Linear Equations in One Variable 2|2.7|4f669597|274|1.2|spr|-|2(p+1)+8(p-1)=5p. What value of p is the solution?|-|SPR: 10p-6=5p so p=1.2
Linear Equations in One Variable 2|2.8|ce314070|489|D|mcq|-|If 4x-1/2=-5, what is the value of 8x-1?|2;-9/8;-5/2;-10|Double the whole equation; A/B/C=solved for x then mis-substituted; D=-10 CORRECT
Linear Equations in One Variable 2|2.9|36ab4122|443|B|mcq|-|Megan earns p dollars per hour for the first 8 hours plus 1.5 times that rate beyond 8 hours. She worked 10 hours and earned 137.50 dollars. What is p?|11.75;12.50;13.25;13.75|8p+2(1.5p)=11p=137.50; A/C=wrong overtime multiplier; D=137.50/10 (ignored overtime); B=CORRECT
Linear Equations in One Variable 2|2.10|5ad9eff0|444|B|mcq|-|A rectangular dance floor has width w feet and length 6 feet longer. Which expresses the perimeter in terms of w?|2w+6;4w+12;w^2+6;w^2+6w|A=one length plus one width only; B=2(w+w+6) CORRECT; C/D=area expressions
Linear Equations in One Variable 2|2.11|45bba652|409|A|mcq|-|If 2(x-5)+3(x-5)=10, what is the value of x-5?|2;5;7;12|5(x-5)=10 so x-5=2; A=CORRECT; B/C/D=solved for x instead
Linear Equations in One Variable 2|2.12|eafdbbbd|395|C|mcq|-|(1/4)(x+5)-(1/3)(x+5)=-7. What value of x is the solution?|-12;-5;79;204|(-1/12)(x+5)=-7 so x+5=84; A/B=sign errors; C=79 CORRECT; D=used 1/4+1/3
Linear Equations in One Variable 2|2.13|8c515062|393|D|mcq|-|A 17-ounce candle loses 1 ounce every 4 hours. If 6 ounces remain, how many hours has it been burning?|3;6;24;44|11 ounces burned times 4 hours; A/B=ounces not hours; C=used the 6 remaining; D=44 CORRECT
Linear Equations in One Variable 2|2.14|ce6b52d8|218|60|spr|-|If 2(3t-10)+t=40+4t, what is the value of 3t?|-|SPR: t=20 so 3t=60
Linear Equations in One Variable 2|2.15|620abf36|369|C|mcq|-|If 5(x+4)=4(x+4)+29, what is the value of x+4?|-4;25;29;33|Treat (x+4) as a unit: it equals 29; A/B=solved for x; C=CORRECT; D=added 4 to 29
Linear Equations in One Variable 2|2.16|76f29fa5|437|C|mcq|-|Boat rental is 950 dollars for the first 2 hours plus 50 dollars per hour after. Total for t hours (t>2) is 1100 dollars. Which equation represents this?|950(t-2)+50t=1100;950(2t)+50t=1100;950+50(t-2)=1100;950+50(2t)=1100|A/B=multiplied the flat fee by time; C=CORRECT; D=doubled the hours instead of subtracting
Linear Equations in One Variable 2|2.17|feb78194|270|37|spr|-|A museum earns 14 dollars per tablet rented, paid 112 dollars of expenses, and made 406 dollars profit. How many tablets were rented?|-|SPR: 14n-112=406 so n=37
Linear Equations in One Variable 2|2.18|018a2704|381|C|mcq|-|If 46=16+2(x-8), what is the value of 2(x-8)?|16;23;30;38|Subtract 16 from both sides; A=copied 16; B=solved for x-8 then added; C=30 CORRECT; D=misc
Linear Equations in One Variable 2|2.19|9d4270fe|499|A|mcq|-|15,000=2.00x-4,500 models monthly profit when x dispensers are sold. Best interpretation of 2.00x?|Monthly sales revenue from selling x dispensers;Revenue from each dispenser sold;Cost of creating each dispenser;Cost of creating x dispensers|2.00x is total revenue for x units; B=describes 2.00 alone; C/D=confuse revenue with cost; A=CORRECT
Linear Equations in One Variable 3|3.1|2937ef4f|491|D|mcq|-|An auger removes corn at a constant rate. A bin had 24,000 bushels; after 5 hours 19,350 remained. Total hours used when 12,840 bushels remain?|3;7;8;12|Rate 930 bushels/hour; 11,160/930=12 total hours; A/B/C=used only the additional time or a wrong rate; D=CORRECT
Linear Equations in One Variable 3|3.2|b7e6394d|562|D|mcq|-|Alan drives 100 miles weekly at 25 mpg; gas costs 4 dollars per gallon. Which equation finds m, the fewer miles needed to save 5 dollars weekly?|(25/4)m=95;(25/4)m=5;(4/25)m=95;(4/25)m=5|Cost per mile is 4/25; savings target is 5; A/C=used 95 (the new total, not the savings); B=inverted the rate; D=CORRECT
Linear Equations in One Variable 3|3.3|e6cb2402|243|16/17|spr|-|3(kx+13)=(48/17)x+36 has no solution. What is the value of k?|-|SPR: 3k=48/17 so k=16/17
Linear Equations in One Variable 3|3.4|ae2287e2|542|A|mcq|-|A product costs 65 dollars to make; commission is 20 percent of the 100 dollar sales price. Which equation gives units u sold for 6,840 dollars profit?|(100(1-0.2)-65)u=6840;(100-65)(1-0.8)u=6840;0.8(100)-65u=6840;(0.2(100)+65)u=6840|Profit per unit is 100-20-65=15; A=CORRECT; B=applied the discount to the margin; C=did not multiply the whole margin by u; D=added commission to cost
Linear Equations in One Variable 3|3.5|771bd0ca|242|-22|spr|-|5(t+3)-7(t+3)=38. What value of t is the solution?|-|SPR: -2(t+3)=38 so t=-22
Linear Equations in One Variable 3|3.6|90095507|1022|B|mcq|table-realty|Glenview Street sold for 140,000 dollars after a 40 percent discount and an additional 20 percent off the discounted price. Which best approximates the original price?|350000;291700;233300;175000|Original times 0.6 times 0.8 = 140000; B=140000/0.48 CORRECT; C=divided by 0.6 only; D=divided by 0.8 only; A=subtracted 60 percent instead
Linear Equations in One Variable 3|3.7|0cb57740|421|B|mcq|-|A 30-sided polygon has sides of three lengths. Sides of length 8 cm number 5 times the n sides of length 3 cm; 6 sides are 4 cm. Which equation must be true for n?|5n+6=30;6n+6=30;8n+3n+4n=30;8(5n)+3n+4(6)=30|Count sides not lengths: 5n+n+6=30; A=omitted the n three-cm sides; B=CORRECT; C/D=weighted by side length instead of counting
Linear Equations in One Variable 3|3.8|aee9fd2d|370|B|mcq|-|If (x+6)/3=(x+6)/13, the value of x+6 is between which pair of values?|-7 and -3;-2 and 2;2 and 7;8 and 13|Two unequal denominators force the numerator to be 0; x+6=0 lies between -2 and 2; B=CORRECT; others assume a nonzero value
Linear Equations in One Variable 3|3.9|3f8a701b|520|D|mcq|roman-numeral|9x+5=a(x+b) has no solutions. Which must be true? I. a=9  II. b=5  III. b is not 5/9|None;I only;I and II only;I and III only|Need a=9 and ab not equal 5 so b not equal 5/9; D=CORRECT; B=omits the constant condition; C=states b=5 which is not required
Linear Equations in One Variable 3|3.10|628300a9|542|C|mcq|-|5 lab stations each use Experiment A (6 tsp salt) or B (4 tsp). If x stations use A, which expression gives total teaspoons of salt?|5x;10x;2x+20;10x+20|6x+4(5-x)=2x+20; A/B=ignored the split; C=CORRECT; D=failed to subtract x from 5
Linear Equations in One Variable 3|3.11|38bf4e04|442|D|mcq|-|A factory makes 9-inch, 7-inch, and 4-inch screws. The 9-inch count is 5 times the number n of 7-inch, and 22 are 4-inch. Total is 100. Which equation represents this?|9(5n)+7n+4(22)=100;9n+7n+4n=100;5n+22=100;6n+22=100|Count screws not inches: 5n+n+22=100; A/B=weighted by length; C=omitted the n seven-inch screws; D=CORRECT
Linear Equations in One Variable 3|3.12|25e1cfed|368|C|mcq|-|How many solutions does 10(15x-9)=-15(6-10x) have?|Exactly one;Exactly two;Infinitely many;Zero|Both sides simplify to 150x-90 so it is an identity; C=CORRECT; A=assumed a unique solution; D=confused with a no-solution case
Linear Equations in One Variable 3|3.13|f5ff91b2|382|B|mcq|-|If (x-5)/7=(x-5)/9, the value of x-5 is between which pair of values?|-9 and -7;-3 and 3;4.5 and 5.5;6.75 and 9.25|Unequal denominators force x-5=0; B=CORRECT; C/D=used the denominators or solved for x instead
Linear Equations in One Variable 3|3.14|429fb7c0|218|-49/150|spr|-|What value of t is the solution to 0.8t-0.46=8(t-0.001)+1.9?|-|SPR: -7.2t=2.352 so t=-49/150
Linear Equations in One Variable 3|3.15|f14484a5|499|D|mcq|-|A plant makes 10-inch, 9-inch, and 7-inch pans. The 10-inch count is 4 times the number n of 9-inch, and 10 are 7-inch. Total is 100. Which equation represents this?|10(4n)+9n+7(10)=100;10n+9n+7n=100;4n+10=100;5n+10=100|Count pans not inches: 4n+n+10=100; A/B=weighted by size; C=omitted the n nine-inch pans; D=CORRECT
Linear Equations in One Variable 3|3.16|ac472881|243|403|spr|-|(12x+28)/4 - s/13 = r(x-8) has infinitely many solutions, s>0. What is the value of s?|-|SPR: r=3 and 7-s/13=-24 so s=403
Linear Equations in Two Variables 1|1.1|ee846db7|442|A|mcq|-|5.48x+7.30y=1,277.94 models yogurt sales where x is smaller containers and y is larger. Which represents the price of each smaller container?|5.48;7.30y;7.30;5.48x|A=the coefficient of x CORRECT; B/D=include the variable (total, not unit price); C=price of the larger container
Linear Equations in Two Variables 1|1.2|5b8a8475|378|A|mcq|-|Line k is y=3x+15. Line j is perpendicular to k. What is the slope of line j?|-1/3;-1/12;-1/18;-1/45|Negative reciprocal of 3; A=CORRECT; B/C/D=used the intercept 15 in the reciprocal
Linear Equations in Two Variables 1|1.3|b23bba4c|499|B|mcq|-|3a+4b=25 relates a small boxes and b large boxes shipped for 25 dollars. If 3 small boxes were shipped, how many large boxes?|3;4;5;6|9+4b=25 so b=4; A=copied the given a; C/D=arithmetic slips; B=CORRECT
