Linear Equations in Two Variables 3|3.19|05bb1af9|805|A|mcq|line-graph-shallow-negative|The graph of y=f(x)+14 has y-intercept 2 and slope -1/4. Which equation defines function f?|f(x)=-(1/4)x-12;f(x)=-(1/4)x+16;f(x)=-(1/4)x+2;f(x)=-(1/4)x-14|Subtract 14 from the graphed intercept; B=added 14 instead; C=read the graph directly without shifting; D=subtracted 14 from 0; A=CORRECT
