Nonlinear Equations and Systems 1|1.6|b76a2815|530|A|mcq|-|P=W/t gives power from work W over time t. Which expresses W in terms of P and t?|W=Pt;W=P/t;W=t/P;W=P+t|Multiply both sides by t; B/C=divided; D=added; A=CORRECT
Nonlinear Equations and Systems 1|1.7|c7789423|242|11, -7|spr|-|What is one possible solution to the equation absolute value of (x-2) equals 9?|-|SPR: x-2=9 or x-2=-9 so x=11 or x=-7; both accepted
Nonlinear Equations and Systems 1|1.8|eb268057|498|A|mcq|-|Which value of x satisfies x^2=64?|-8;4;32;128|x=8 or -8; B=took a quarter; C=halved; D=doubled; A=CORRECT
Nonlinear Functions 1|1.1|6abec9a8|795|B|mcq|exponential-decay-graph|An exponential curve rises from below toward a horizontal asymptote at y=-4 and crosses the y-axis at -5. What is the y-intercept of the graph shown?|(-1,-9);(0,-5);(0,-4);(0,0)|The y-intercept is where x=0; A=used a different point; C=gave the asymptote; D=assumed the origin; B=CORRECT
Nonlinear Functions 1|1.2|1ee962ec|1047|C|mcq|parabola-ocean-water-table|A parabola models ocean water level over 6 hours with zeros at x=0 and x=6 and vertex (3,-12). Which table gives x values and their corresponding y values?|(0,-12),(0,3),(3,6);(0,0),(3,12),(0,-6);(0,0),(3,-12),(6,0);(0,0),(12,3),(-6,0)|C=matches the zeros and vertex CORRECT; A/B=sign errors or repeated x values; D=swapped coordinates
Nonlinear Functions 1|1.3|788bfd56|370|B|mcq|-|The function f is defined by f(x)=4+sqrt(x). What is the value of f(144)?|0;16;40;76|sqrt144=12 so 4+12=16; A=subtracted; C/D=multiplied instead of adding; B=CORRECT
Nonlinear Functions 1|1.4|b39d74a0|1189|B|mcq|graph-choices-cubic|A table gives (0,0),(1,1),(2,8),(3,27). Which graph could represent this relationship?|decreasing cubic;increasing cubic through the origin;shifted cubic;steep curve not through the origin|The data are y=x^3, increasing through the origin; A=negative leading coefficient; C/D=wrong intercept or shape; B=CORRECT
One-Variable Data 1|1.1|f890dc20|425|B|mcq|-|What is the median of the seven data values 2, 2, 2, 3, 4, 4, 11?|2;3;4;9|The middle value of seven sorted numbers is the fourth; A=the mode; C=a common value; D=the range; B=CORRECT
One-Variable Data 1|1.2|8736334b|444|C|mcq|-|Data set A is 72, 73, 73, 76, 76 and data set B is 61, 64, 74, 85, x. If the means are equal, what is x?|77;85;86;95|Mean A is 74 so the sum of B must be 370 giving x=86; A/B/D=arithmetic slips; C=CORRECT
One-Variable Data 1|1.3|c88e0663|395|A|mcq|-|10 students sold a total of 90 boxes of cookies. Which can be calculated from this information?|Average boxes sold per student;Median boxes per student;Greatest number sold by one student;Least number sold by one student|Only the mean follows from a total and a count; B/C/D=require the individual values; A=CORRECT
One-Variable Data 1|1.4|12dae628|393|B|mcq|-|What is the mean of the data 2, 9, 14, 23, 32?|14;16;17;32|Sum 80 divided by 5; A=the median; C=misc; D=the maximum; B=CORRECT
One-Variable Data 1|1.5|fa7a0164|510|A|mcq|table-temperatures|A table gives high and low temperatures for five days; lows are 49, 37, 41, 54, 63. What was the mean low temperature?|48.8;49;59;59.1|Sum 244 divided by 5; B=the median-ish value; C/D=used the high temperatures; A=CORRECT
One-Variable Data 1|1.6|708590d7|446|D|mcq|-|Data set A is 1 through 7 and data set B is 1,1,2,2,3,3,4. Which statement correctly compares the means?|Each mean is 2;Each mean is 4;Mean of A is less than mean of B;Mean of A is greater than mean of B|Mean A is 4 and mean B is about 2.29; A/B=assumed equality; C=reversed; D=CORRECT
One-Variable Data 1|1.7|374b18f9|503|B|mcq|box-plot-timberland|A box plot summarizes acres of timberland in 13 counties. Which is closest to the median number of acres?|4399;7067;8831;10595|Read the line inside the box; A=read Q1; C=read Q3; D=read the maximum; B=CORRECT
Percentages 1|1.1|bd90f87e|856|B|mcq|table-minimum-wage|A table gives US minimum wage by year including 1.00 in 1960 and 1.60 in 1970. What was the percent increase from 1960 to 1970?|30;60;62.5;120|Increase 0.60 over the original 1.00; A=halved; C=divided by the new value; D=doubled; B=CORRECT
Percentages 1|1.2|8705ecba|394|C|mcq|-|A shirt costs 20 dollars before a 5 percent sales tax. What is the total cost including tax?|20.05;20.50;21.00;25.00|20 times 1.05; A=added 5 cents; B=used 2.5 percent; D=added 5 dollars; C=CORRECT
Percentages 1|1.3|191d167b|393|B|mcq|-|Last year 200 students enrolled; this year enrollment is 147 percent of last year. How many are enrolled this year?|247;294;347;394|200 times 1.47; A=added 47; C=added 147; D=doubled the answer; B=CORRECT
Percentages 1|1.4|bb7c8186|369|A|mcq|-|What is 23 percent of 100?|23;46;77;123|0.23 times 100; B=doubled; C=the complement; D=added to 100; A=CORRECT
Percentages 1|1.5|949cd96b|393|D|mcq|-|The base of a parallelogram is 89 percent of the height h. Which expression represents the base?|89h;0.089h;8.9h;0.89h|Convert the percent to a decimal; A=used the whole number; B/C=shifted the decimal wrongly; D=CORRECT
Probability 1|1.1|1353b86e|763|D|mcq|table-marbles|A table shows 8 red, 10 blue, 22 green marbles, total 40. What is the probability a randomly chosen marble is blue?|30/40;22/40;18/40;10/40|Favorable over total; A=complement of blue; B=green count; C=red plus green minus something; D=CORRECT
Probability 1|1.2|d89c1513|746|D|mcq|two-way-table-gas-beverage|A two-way table of 135 gas station customers shows 85 purchased gasoline and 50 did not. What is the probability a random customer did not purchase gasoline?|15/50;15/40;35/50;50/135|Row total over grand total; A/B/C=used a cell instead of the row total or the wrong denominator; D=CORRECT
