Ratios, Rates, Proportions, and Units 1|1.7|6310adbc|401|D|mcq|-|The ratio of t to u is 1 to 2 and t=10. What is the value of u?|2;5;10;20|u=2t=20; A=copied the ratio term; B=halved instead of doubling; C=copied t; D=CORRECT
Sample Statistics and Margin of Error 1|1.1|90eed2e5|473|C|mcq|-|A random sample of 20 of 50 city council members found 6 supporters. Best estimate of the number of supporters among all 50?|6;9;15;30|6/20 of 50 = 15; A=the sample count; B=misc; D=used a half; C=CORRECT
Sample Statistics and Margin of Error 1|1.2|e7d9649f|451|B|mcq|-|In a random sample of 50 from a town of 14,878, 7 named chocolate. About how many in the town would name chocolate?|350;2100;7500;10500|7/50 of 14,878 is about 2,083; A=multiplied 7 by 50; C/D=used a far larger proportion; B=CORRECT
Sample Statistics and Margin of Error 1|1.3|f4b3672a|494|C|mcq|-|A 253-acre forest is sampled with five 1-acre parcels having 51, 59, 45, 52, 73 trees. Which range contains the best estimate of total trees?|11000 to 12000;12500 to 13500;13500 to 14500;18000 to 19000|Mean 56 times 253 is 14,168; A/B=used a lower mean; D=used the maximum parcel; C=CORRECT
Sample Statistics and Margin of Error 1|1.4|0108ac2d|515|C|mcq|-|300 randomly selected students gave 38 percent support with a 5.5 percent margin of error. Best interpretation?|Percent is exactly 38;Percent is greater than 38;Plausible values are between 32.5 and 43.5;Plausible numbers are between 295 and 305|C=estimate plus or minus the margin CORRECT; A=treats the estimate as exact; B=one-sided; D=applies the margin to the sample size
Sample Statistics and Margin of Error 1|1.5|6a305cd0|420|C|mcq|-|A random sample had a mean of 37 with a margin of error of 3. Most appropriate conclusion about the population mean?|Less than 37;Greater than 37;Between 34 and 40;Less than 34 or greater than 40|C=CORRECT; A/B=one-sided; D=inverts the interval
Sample Statistics and Margin of Error 1|1.6|2c76bcce|487|A|mcq|-|Estimated mean handbag weight is 27.8 oz with a margin of error of 0.02 oz. Most plausible conclusion?|Mean of all handbags is between 27.78 and 27.82;Actual weights of all handbags are between 27.78 and 27.82;Actual weights in the sample are between 27.78 and 27.82;Mean is exactly 27.8|A=the interval estimates the MEAN CORRECT; B/C=apply the interval to individual values; D=treats the estimate as exact
